# BNote Development Rules

## ⚠️ MOST IMPORTANT RULE - READ THIS FIRST ⚠️

**🚫 NEVER MODIFY ANY CODE OUTSIDE THE `/bnote-next-generation/` FOLDER 🚫**

**ABSOLUTE PROHIBITION:**
- ❌ **DO NOT** touch `/BNote/src/` directory (old PHP codebase)
- ❌ **DO NOT** modify `/BNote/main.php`, `/BNote/content.php`, or any files in `/BNote/` folder
- ❌ **DO NOT** change any files outside `/bnote-next-generation/` folder
- ❌ **DO NOT** refactor, update, modernize, or improve old codebase
- ❌ **DO NOT** fix bugs in old code (unless explicitly requested for critical security)
- ❌ **DO NOT** add features to old codebase
- ❌ **DO NOT** update dependencies for old codebase

**✅ ONLY ALLOWED:**
- ✅ Work **ONLY** in `/bnote-next-generation/` directory
- ✅ Modify files **ONLY** within `/bnote-next-generation/` folder
- ✅ Read old codebase for reference (but never modify)
- ✅ Use old codebase classes/functions via API calls (but never change them)
- ✅ Use `BNOTE_ROOT` constant (defined in `bnote-next-generation/api/paths.php`) to reference old codebase

**This is the #1 priority rule. If you're unsure, DON'T modify it. Ask the user first.**

## Project Context
This is BNote - an open source ensemble management system for bands, orchestras, and choirs.
- **Architecture:** 3-tier MVC (data/logic/presentation)
- **Old UI:** PHP-generated HTML with inline CSS (`/BNote/src/presentation/`) - **READ ONLY**
- **New UI:** BNote Next Generation - Modern JavaScript SPA (`/bnote-next-generation/`) - **ONLY MODIFY THIS**
- **License:** GPL-3.0 (all code must remain GPL-compliant)

## Project Structure

```
/bnote/
├── BNote/                      ← Old codebase (NEVER MODIFY)
│   ├── src/
│   ├── main.php
│   └── config/
└── bnote-next-generation/      ← New app (ONLY MODIFY THIS)
    ├── api/
    ├── assets/
    └── docs/
```

## Protected Directories (NEVER MODIFY)

**Complete list of off-limits directories:**
- `/BNote/src/` - All old PHP code (data, logic, presentation) - **READ ONLY**
- `/BNote/main.php` - Old entry point - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- `/BNote/content.php` - Old layout - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- `/BNote/index.php` - Old routing - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- `/BNote/components/` - Old JavaScript components - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- `/BNote/style/` - Old CSS/styles - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- `/BNote/lib/` - Old libraries - **DO NOT TOUCH**
- Any file or directory outside `/bnote-next-generation/` - **DO NOT TOUCH**

**Exception:** Only modify old code if user explicitly requests it for critical security fixes AND confirms in writing.

## Core Principles

### 1. Code Style (Next Generation Only)
- Use modern JavaScript (ES6+)
- Use English variable names (no German)
- Use meaningful, descriptive names
- Keep indentation consistent
- Add comments for complex logic

### 2. Browser Compatibility
- Target modern browsers (last 2 versions)
- No IE11 support needed
- Progressive enhancement approach
- Use standard HTML5/CSS3

### 3. Internationalization (i18n) - MANDATORY

**CRITICAL:** ALL user-facing strings MUST use the i18n system. No hardcoded text.

**For Next Generation UI (`/bnote-next-generation/`):**
- **HTML:** Use `data-i18n`, `data-i18n-placeholder`, `data-i18n-label` attributes
- **JavaScript:** Always use `i18n.t(key)` for user-facing strings
- **Translation Files:** Add keys to all language files (`bnote-next-generation/lang/*.json`)
- **Key Format:** `js.{module}.{key}` (e.g., `js.dashboard.welcome`)
- **Never hardcode:** No English, German, or other language strings in code
- **German text:** Only exists in `bnote-next-generation/lang/de.json` (translation file)

**Examples:**
```html
<!-- GOOD -->
<h1 data-i18n="js.dashboard.welcome">Welcome</h1>
<input data-i18n-placeholder="js.login.usernamePlaceholder" />

<!-- BAD -->
<h1>Welcome</h1>
<input placeholder="Username" />
```

```javascript
// GOOD
showToast(i18n.t('js.users.created'));
const errorMsg = i18n.t('js.error.loadFailed');

// BAD
showToast('User created');
const errorMsg = 'Failed to load';
```

### 4. Dark Mode Support - MANDATORY

**CRITICAL:** ALL UI components MUST support dark mode.

**CSS Variables:**
- Use semantic color variables from `next/assets/css/app.css`
- Variables automatically adapt to dark mode via `.dark` class
- Never hardcode colors

**Tailwind Classes:**
```html
<!-- GOOD - Uses semantic variables -->
<div class="bg-background text-foreground">
  <div class="bg-card border border-border">
    <p class="text-muted-foreground">Text</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- BAD - Hardcoded colors -->
<div class="bg-white text-black dark:bg-gray-800 dark:text-white">
```

**Theme Toggle:**
- Use `ThemeToggle.toggle()` to switch themes
- Theme preference saved in localStorage
- Respects system preference on first load

**Testing:**
- Always test components in both light and dark modes
- Use browser dev tools to toggle dark mode

### 5. License Compliance

- All code must remain GPL-3.0
- **MANDATORY:** Add GPL v3 license headers to all source files in `/next/`
- Use standard Tailwind patterns (MIT licensed)
- Avoid copying proprietary UI components
- Keep GPL headers in all modified files

## Next Generation UI Development

**Location:** `/bnote-next-generation/` directory ONLY

**Key Requirements:**
1. **MANDATORY i18n:** All user-facing strings must use `i18n.t()` or `data-i18n` attributes
2. **MANDATORY Dark Mode:** All components must use semantic CSS variables
3. **GPL Headers:** All source files must include GPL v3 license headers
4. **API Pattern:** Use module-based API (`/bnote-next-generation/api/index.php?module=X&action=Y`)
5. **Translation Files:** Add keys to all language files (`bnote-next-generation/lang/*.json`)
6. **Path Configuration:** Use `BNOTE_ROOT` constant (from `bnote-next-generation/api/paths.php`) to reference old codebase

**Technology Stack:**
- Vanilla JavaScript (no frameworks)
- Tailwind CSS (via CDN)
- Lucide Icons (via CDN)
- Custom i18n service (`next/assets/js/i18n.js`)
- Theme toggle (`next/assets/js/theme-toggle.js`)

**See:** [bnote-next-generation/README.md](bnote-next-generation/README.md) for architecture details

## Workflow

**For Next Generation UI (`/bnote-next-generation/`):**
1. All user-facing strings must use i18n
2. All components must support dark mode
3. Use semantic CSS variables for colors
4. Test in both light and dark modes
5. Add translation keys to all language files
6. Add GPL v3 headers to all new/modified files

## Next Generation UI Examples

### Example: Component with i18n and Dark Mode

```html
<!-- GOOD - Uses i18n and semantic colors -->
<div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-lg p-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-card-foreground mb-4" 
        data-i18n="js.dashboard.welcome">Welcome</h2>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground" data-i18n="js.dashboard.subtitle">Welcome to %p</p>
    <button class="bg-primary text-primary-foreground px-4 py-2 rounded-lg"
            data-i18n-label="js.common.save">Save</button>
</div>
```

```javascript
// GOOD - Uses i18n for all strings
const Dashboard = {
    async loadData() {
        try {
            const data = await DashboardApi.getDashboard();
            this.render(data);
        } catch (error) {
            // Use i18n for error message
            showToast(i18n.t('js.error.dashboardLoadFailed'));
        }
    },
    
    render(data) {
        // All text uses i18n
        container.innerHTML = `
            <h1 data-i18n="js.dashboard.welcome">Welcome</h1>
            <div class="bg-card border border-border">
                <!-- Content -->
            </div>
        `;
        // Translate after rendering
        i18n.translatePage();
    }
};
```

## Priority Order

**Next Generation:**
1. Complete localization for existing modules
2. Implement remaining modules (Calendar, Messages, etc.)
3. Add advanced features (search, exports, etc.)

## Testing Reminders

- Test in Chrome/Firefox (latest)
- Check mobile responsiveness (narrow browser window)
- Verify all buttons/links still work
- No JavaScript errors in console
- Forms still submit correctly
- Test in both light and dark modes

## Notes

- Cursor should generate clean, readable code
- Preserve existing functionality 100%
- For Next Generation: Always use i18n and support dark mode
- **NEVER modify old codebase** - work only in `/bnote-next-generation/` directory
